1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,520
<i>Maybe forgetting me</i>

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,000
<i>would be better than having</i>
<i>to hate someone as awful as me.</i>

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:08,720
<i>Finito amora!</i>

4
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,480
Khobfa.

5
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,000
Why did you give me my bracelet back?

6
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:13,800
Wait.

7
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:18,680
You remember me?

8
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,720
Of course I do.

9
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:23,640
Really?

10
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:27,120
Then do you remember what I did to you?

11
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:32,840
After what you did to me,
how could I ever forget?

12
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:37,160
Khobfa.

13
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:42,760
Do you know
the kind of person I hate the most?

14
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,800
Someone who does something wrong
but won't own up to it.

15
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:50,720
Someone who's been lying to me
all this time like you.

16
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,960
Mark my words.

17
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,760
I'll hate you forever.

18
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:11,720
<i>I hate people who do something wrong</i>
<i>but won't own up to it.</i>

19
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:14,520
<i>Someone who's been lying to me</i>
<i>all this time like you.</i>

20
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,880
<i>I'll hate you forever.</i>

21
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,760
How are you holding up?

22
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:29,640
We're here to take you to class.

23
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:33,080
I'm not feeling well.
I don't think I'll go.

24
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:38,320
Hey, you can't keep hiding forever.

25
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:45,120
How am I supposed to face everyone
after the shit I've done?

26
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:48,680
Hey, don't worry.

27
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:49,960
We've got your back.

28
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,360
But…

29
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,760
Or are you afraid to face Khobfa?

30
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,480
That's not an issue.

31
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,960
Khobfa doesn't remember me anymore.

32
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:07,680
Why?

33
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,800
I broke the curse.

34
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,959
Khobfa doesn't remember me anymore.

35
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:24,160
Damn, Rin.

36
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,560
You never know.

37
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,400
Maybe the curse wasn't even real.

38
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,800
He might still remember you.

39
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:53,440
Hey, I forgot to get something.

40
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:56,280
I'll go buy it. Wait here.
We'll head up to class together.

41
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,440
Come on, Ohm.

42
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:58,880
- Me?
- Come with me.

43
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:07,840
Hey.

44
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,280
<i>Maybe the curse wasn't even real.</i>

45
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:31,480
<i>Khobfa might still remember you.</i>

46
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:42,840
Watch where you're going.

47
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,760
Shit.

48
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:56,000
Khobfa really doesn't remember you
after all that time you spent together.

49
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,760
Okay, that's all for today.

50
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:07,600
- See you next time. Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

51
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,520
It's okay, man.

52
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:34,080
All they can do is talk.
They can't do anything to us.

53
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:36,840
Exactly. This is not a big deal.

54
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,400
People will forget soon enough.

55
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,640
Krit and Mochi are lucky
they didn't show up today.

56
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:42,480
I would've punched them.

57
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,760
Yeah, I would've punched them too.

58
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,160
Great job.

59
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,120
Nice.

60
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:56,920
<i>Khobfa really doesn't remember you</i>
<i>after all that time you spent together.</i>

61
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:02,120
Hello, guys.

62
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,680
Hi.

63
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:08,200
Khobfa, you remember us?

64
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:12,560
Of course I do. I don't have amnesia.

65
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,200
See you in the rehearsal room.

66
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:15,360
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

67
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,920
Hey, wait.

68
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,400
You remember the band competition too?

69
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:23,000
What's with you? We made it through
the first round together.

70
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,480
Of course I remember.

71
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:27,160
The final competition is coming up.
Make sure you practice hard.

72
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:31,920
Wait. If you really remember,
name everyone in the band.

73
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:37,120
What is it now? Well, there's you two.

74
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:38,960
Then me,

75
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,760
and…

76
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,760
Danthai. Four of us.

77
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:54,040
Is that really all you remember?
What about…

78
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,840
Hey.

79
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:07,120
Your shoelace is untied.

80
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:23,080
So you're really the only one
he doesn't remember, Rin.

81
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,400
Yeah, seriously.

82
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:27,280
Do we still have to compete
in the competition?

83
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:29,640
Hey, you have to keep going.

84
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:32,799
You have to lead the band to victory.

85
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:43,200
I just want Khobfa to finally see
his dream come true just once.

86
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:54,680
Mochi, please open the door.

87
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,720
I know you heard me. Open the door.

88
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:06,680
Mochi.

89
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,520
Mochi.

90
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,280
Hi, everyone.

91
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,120
I'm Mochi.

92
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:33,000
<i>I'm going live today</i>

93
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:36,360
to apologize to someone.

94
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,520
Hey.

95
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,960
- What are you watching?
- Mochi's live.

96
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,600
Someone I feel…

97
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,480
really guilty about hurting.

98
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:52,360
<i>But I don't know if he'll forgive me.</i>

99
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:00,520
Rin.

100
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,560
I'm really sorry.

101
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:09,880
<i>I'm the one who edited the clip</i>
<i>to make it look worse than it was.</i>

102
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:12,600
<i>Then I gave the file to the staff team.</i>

103
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:16,480
<i>I just wanted you to hurt the way I did</i>

104
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,600
<i>when you betrayed me</i>
<i>by getting together with Krit.</i>

105
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,760
<i>I just wanted to teach you a lesson.</i>

106
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:28,040
<i>But I never thought</i>
<i>it would hurt you this badly.</i>

107
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,640
I'm really sorry.

108
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:10,600
THE WINNERS OF THE UNIVERSITY'S
2026 KOL CONTEST

109
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,240
Congratulations.

110
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:35,560
I'm sorry…

111
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:41,240
for ruining your life like that.

112
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:53,360
Some good actually came out of it.

113
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:58,880
It helped me decide to do something
I should've done a long time ago.

114
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,320
I was…

115
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,400
so damn selfish.

116
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:07,960
So…

117
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,440
I should probably thank you for that clip.

118
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:17,840
It pushed me to make things right,

119
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:22,920
removing something bad from Khobfa's life.

120
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,960
Remember back in high school?

121
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,680
We made a rule for our group.

122
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:44,440
We'd stay strong
in front of the rest of the world.

123
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,760
But with each other,
we could let our guard down

124
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,560
because…

125
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:55,240
- we're friends.
- We're friends.

126
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:09,240
You don't have to be strong around me…

127
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:13,440
my friend.

128
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,920
Ow! Shit!

129
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,560
You again?

130
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:57,520
Why do I keep running into you?

131
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:59,200
Got feelings for me or something?

132
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:01,400
Huh?

133
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:02,560
No.

134
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:08,880
Wait.

135
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:32,640
Thanks a lot.

136
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,160
That was close.

137
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:40,040
If I'd lost this,
I wouldn't have been able to sleep.

138
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:44,280
Is it pretty?

139
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:50,200
Yeah, it is.

140
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:53,760
I feel really attached to it.

141
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:57,000
Who gave it to me?

142
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:13,320
Hey! My clothes!

143
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,680
Hey, where are you taking them?

144
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:20,560
Here.

145
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,720
Hurry up and get on.

146
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,640
Come on. I'll give you a ride.

147
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:36,920
<i>Maybe it is better</i>
<i>that Khobfa has forgotten me.</i>

148
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:40,240
<i>If it means</i>
<i>he won't have bad luck anymore,</i>

149
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:44,280
<i>then I think it's worth it.</i>

150
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:00,400
I'm sorry.

151
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:03,480
Hold on tight. Don't fall off again.

152
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:05,960
Why does this route feel so familiar?

153
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:08,280
It's like I used
to come this way all the time.

154
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:12,840
These streets all look alike.

155
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,680
Turn left over there.

156
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:17,600
Turn left.

157
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:29,120
Here, let me help.

158
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,520
Hey, you don't have to.

159
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,600
Let me do it.

160
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:42,280
Why does this feel so familiar? It's like
I've dropped someone off here before.

161
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:45,880
Really?

162
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:47,800
What's your name again?

163
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:52,280
Rin.

164
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,200
I'm Khobfa.

165
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:57,160
Nice to meet you.

166
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:01,880
Nice to meet you…

167
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:04,760
Khobfa.

168
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:15,720
I'll get going.

169
00:17:17,599 --> 00:17:18,800
<i>That goes for you too.</i>

170
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:20,520
<i>About Khobfa.</i>

171
00:17:20,599 --> 00:17:23,000
You still have the right to love him.

172
00:17:23,599 --> 00:17:25,200
If you can forgive me,

173
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,600
I think Khobfa can forgive you too.

174
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:39,880
Hey, wait.

175
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:41,960
My stuff.

176
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:44,680
Oh, I almost forgot.

177
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,280
Here.

178
00:17:58,600 --> 00:17:59,440
Thanks.

179
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:01,280
Yeah.

180
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:14,800
So you're saying Khobfa ran into you
and then gave you a ride here?

181
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:17,120
- That's one hell of a coincidence.
- Right?

182
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:22,840
It's like I'm starting over
with the same person.

183
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:24,640
I'm rooting for you, Rin.

184
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:27,800
What good would starting over do?

185
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:33,760
I'd still have to tell him the truth
about what I did to him.

186
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,520
Then just tell him yourself.

187
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:39,120
Tell him you're sorry.

188
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:41,880
Maybe Khobfa will forgive you.

189
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:48,840
And what if he doesn't?

190
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,960
I'd rather he forgot me

191
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:58,800
than hate me.

192
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,360
Finally, you show up.

193
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:18,720
It's good you came.
I have to clear things up with you.

194
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,400
So do I. You go first.

195
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,720
I think it's time
we ended things between us.

196
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:30,720
We won the university's KOL contest.

197
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,080
So I guess our mission is done.

198
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,080
Mochi.

199
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:40,640
What about our band?

200
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,720
I've damaged the band's reputation.

201
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:46,360
Replace me with whoever you want.
I won't object.

202
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,280
Mochi.

203
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:55,960
I've said what I needed to say.
You can leave now.

204
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:01,120
And let's not see each other anymore.

205
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:13,160
Aren't you going to hear
what I have to say?

206
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:16,760
What is it?

207
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,200
I saw your apology video to Rin.

208
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:30,160
You've sorted things out with him.

209
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:31,720
As for the band,

210
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:34,760
you're staying.

211
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:37,400
Krit,

212
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:42,000
why would you want to keep me
after the shit I did?

213
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,680
What if your band loses because of me?

214
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:45,960
I don't know.

215
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,280
You talked me into starting a band.

216
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:52,160
Now we've made it to the final round.

217
00:20:52,240 --> 00:20:55,240
You're responsible for it.
Look after our band until the end.

218
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,600
But I…

219
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:04,720
You can't quit.

220
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:30,560
KHOBFA'S BIRTHDAY
FINAL ROUND

221
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,120
VICTORY

222
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:37,480
Hey!

223
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:39,640
You scared me.

224
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:42,120
Are you really not coming to watch?

225
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,240
I think I'd better not.
There's someone I don't want to see.

226
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:48,040
But it's the final round.

227
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:49,400
Exactly.

228
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:53,240
You can still change your mind, Rin.
You built this band from scratch.

229
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:54,520
That's right.

230
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,560
I'll watch the live stream.

231
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:06,080
I'll be cheering you on from here.
You guys can do this. Trust me.

232
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:10,480
Oh, and remind everyone in the band
to wear the shirts I had made.

233
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:12,080
Every single member, okay?

234
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:13,320
Yes, sir.

235
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,120
Come on. Bring it in.

236
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,480
Let's get fired up.

237
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:20,800
Horizon!

238
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,240
Yeah.

239
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:27,320
- Horizon, let's go!
- Horizon, let's go!

240
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:32,680
THE 5 FINALIST BANDS!

241
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,640
SAKIT, FRIENDS WITH DEADLINES,
STAND STILL, HORIZON, THE WINNER

242
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:51,760
I still can't reach Khobfa.

243
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:54,040
Just calm down.

244
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:56,120
He had something to take care of.
He'll be here soon.

245
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:00,160
Good luck, guys.

246
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:03,760
Don't try to butter us up, Mochi.

247
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:06,920
Rin may have told us
you two have sorted things out,

248
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,520
but I won't forgive you that easily.

249
00:23:09,120 --> 00:23:13,640
Yeah. After what you did to our friend,
you won't get our forgiveness that easily.

250
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:19,480
I've set myself a minimum of 10,000 hours
to stay mad at you.

251
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:20,520
Remember that.

252
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:24,360
Yeah. I'll make sure I never forget.

253
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:28,960
Where's Khobfa? I wanted to wish him luck.

254
00:23:29,560 --> 00:23:32,160
He's on his way.
He said he'd be a little late.

255
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:34,080
He's taking his time, huh?

256
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:38,120
It's almost time. Let's get ready.

257
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:47,400
So what now? What is Khobfa off doing?

258
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:58,760
<i>Tell him you're sorry.</i>

259
00:23:58,840 --> 00:24:00,920
<i>Maybe Khobfa will forgive you.</i>

260
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,200
<i>Mark my words.</i>

261
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:05,000
I'll hate you forever.

262
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:13,720
Rin!

263
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,040
Mom!

264
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:18,120
Hi, son!

265
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:20,120
Hungry?

266
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:21,760
Come and eat.

267
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:24,640
Thanks.

268
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:30,480
Why did you come back, Mom?
I thought you were heading to Tibet next.

269
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:34,920
Something told me
I should come back to see you.

270
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:40,360
Now, give Ms. Daran a little recap.

271
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:43,240
How's life treating Mr. Darin?

272
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:53,240
Mom.

273
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:55,120
Yeah?

274
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:58,320
I have something to confess.

275
00:25:00,280 --> 00:25:03,720
When I called you
about lifting that curse,

276
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,720
actually…

277
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:10,840
I was the one who cast it.

278
00:25:14,840 --> 00:25:18,240
When you said your friend
had cursed the wrong person?

279
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:19,960
Yes.

280
00:25:22,040 --> 00:25:25,280
And how do you feel about it now?

281
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:34,600
Terrible.

282
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:40,760
I tried to make up for what I'd done.

283
00:25:42,880 --> 00:25:47,040
<i>I found a way to get close to him</i>
<i>and hide everything from him.</i>

284
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:53,520
But he was so good to me.

285
00:25:56,800 --> 00:26:01,000
<i>We started having feelings for each other.</i>

286
00:26:04,280 --> 00:26:08,120
<i>But then something happened.</i>

287
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:11,080
Is what you said

288
00:26:12,040 --> 00:26:13,600
in that video true?

289
00:26:15,120 --> 00:26:16,760
<i>He found out the truth,</i>

290
00:26:18,240 --> 00:26:22,480
<i>so I decided to lift the curse</i>

291
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:25,520
<i>even though it meant</i>
<i>he'd forget everything we'd been through.</i>

292
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:29,920
It might sound selfish,

293
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:34,680
but I just…

294
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:40,800
I was just scared that
if he remembered me…

295
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:44,920
he'd hate me.

296
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:51,320
I sound awful, don't I, Mom?

297
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:02,640
A little.

298
00:27:06,280 --> 00:27:10,960
Good thing my son is so handsome.

299
00:27:11,040 --> 00:27:13,040
That makes you a little less awful.

300
00:27:24,120 --> 00:27:25,000
Here you are.

301
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:33,440
There's one thing I want to tell you.

302
00:27:34,040 --> 00:27:35,400
If you get the chance,

303
00:27:38,360 --> 00:27:40,520
you should tell him the truth.

304
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:43,920
But what if I tell him

305
00:27:45,520 --> 00:27:47,400
and he doesn't forgive me?

306
00:27:53,360 --> 00:27:55,800
At least you'll be able
to forgive yourself,

307
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:58,160
unlike me.

308
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:01,640
I've been living with guilt all this time.

309
00:28:05,160 --> 00:28:09,680
Your dad didn't actually die
in an accident.

310
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:12,920
He probably couldn't accept

311
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:17,000
that I'd taken over
your grandma's spiritual practice.

312
00:28:18,480 --> 00:28:20,600
That's why he left us.

313
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:27,240
I wasn't that concerned about him.

314
00:28:27,840 --> 00:28:29,400
You were the one…

315
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:34,680
I cared about.

316
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:39,880
So I decided not to tell you the truth…

317
00:28:43,120 --> 00:28:45,680
because I was afraid you'd hate me.

318
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:47,640
Mom.

319
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:52,760
The more afraid I was that you'd hate me…

320
00:28:58,960 --> 00:29:02,080
the more I hated myself.

321
00:29:02,760 --> 00:29:04,720
I'm sorry, Rin.

322
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:09,240
I'm sorry I've been lying to you
all this time.

323
00:29:17,320 --> 00:29:18,600
Mom.

324
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:22,000
You don't have to feel guilty anymore.

325
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,800
I like who I am.

326
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:29,720
I love our family just as it is.

327
00:29:32,760 --> 00:29:37,280
Not once, Mom, have I ever felt unloved.

328
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:42,280
You're the best mom in the world,
you know that?

329
00:29:47,520 --> 00:29:48,720
I love you, Mom.

330
00:30:14,440 --> 00:30:16,400
I love you too, sweetheart.

331
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:22,600
If you're not mad that I spoke the truth,

332
00:30:25,360 --> 00:30:30,560
I believe Khobfa will understand
what you've done.

333
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:39,280
So, what are you still sitting here for?

334
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:41,560
Hurry up and go see Khobfa.

335
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:44,040
You're right, Mom.

336
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:49,600
If I leave now, I should still make it.

337
00:30:52,440 --> 00:30:55,120
I'll get going, then. I love you, Mom.

338
00:30:56,720 --> 00:30:59,440
Wait! Don't go yet. Hold on, sweetheart.

339
00:30:59,520 --> 00:31:02,160
You don't have to worry
about the curse in that book anymore.

340
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:04,440
None of it is real.

341
00:31:04,520 --> 00:31:07,200
Huh? That owl spellbook?

342
00:31:07,280 --> 00:31:08,600
It's a mock-up.

343
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:12,200
I thought it was cute,
so I bought it for you.

344
00:31:12,280 --> 00:31:16,200
What about that conversation
I overheard you and Grandma having?

345
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:18,400
About me inheriting the spiritual gifts?

346
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:23,080
Grandma meant Danthai, sweetheart.

347
00:31:23,160 --> 00:31:24,000
What?

348
00:31:24,920 --> 00:31:27,920
But if the curse wasn't real,

349
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:31,680
why couldn't Khobfa remember me
after I lifted it?

350
00:31:31,760 --> 00:31:33,600
I can't tell you that.

351
00:31:33,680 --> 00:31:36,520
You'll have to ask Khobfa yourself.

352
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:46,960
<i>It's still you, as it's always been</i>

353
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:51,120
<i>It's only you, and it'll forever be</i>

354
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:57,160
<i>The emptier I feel</i>
<i>The more I yearn for you</i>

355
00:31:57,240 --> 00:31:59,120
How's everything going, guys?
Where's Khobfa?

356
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:01,680
We have no idea where Khobfa went.
I tried calling, but his phone's off.

357
00:32:01,760 --> 00:32:02,720
What?

358
00:32:02,800 --> 00:32:05,080
We're supposed to play
right after Krit's band.

359
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:06,720
Is Khobfa really abandoning us?

360
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:12,640
<i>This song still resonates in my heart</i>

361
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:40,160
And that was the Winner!

362
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:43,640
How did you feel?

363
00:32:43,720 --> 00:32:47,400
Wow, I felt that performance
resonate in my heart.

364
00:32:47,480 --> 00:32:49,680
- They really gave it their all.
- Yes.

365
00:32:53,760 --> 00:32:56,800
And now, it's time for our final band
of the final round.

366
00:32:56,880 --> 00:33:00,560
- Let's hear it for Horizon!
- Horizon!

367
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:11,120
A round of applause for Horizon!

368
00:33:17,640 --> 00:33:19,640
Let's set up the equipment while we wait.

369
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:21,720
Yeah. Let's get it ready.

370
00:33:29,120 --> 00:33:30,400
Where is he?

371
00:33:33,480 --> 00:33:35,760
It's their turn already, isn't it?

372
00:33:35,840 --> 00:33:38,120
Yeah. They're going onstage
any minute now.

373
00:33:38,200 --> 00:33:39,840
The singer hasn't arrived?

374
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:56,600
- How did he get onstage?
- Yeah, exactly.

375
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:58,280
Where's the actual singer?

376
00:33:58,800 --> 00:34:00,600
Wait, who's this guy?

377
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:02,160
I've never seen him before.

378
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:04,880
Then why is he up there?

379
00:34:05,400 --> 00:34:07,480
Did they change singers
at the last minute?

380
00:34:07,560 --> 00:34:09,080
I don't think so.

381
00:34:09,600 --> 00:34:11,199
Then where did the singer go?

382
00:34:12,199 --> 00:34:13,199
Khobfa!

383
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:16,000
Where are you?

384
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:21,520
Are you not coming onstage
because you're still mad at me?

385
00:34:22,679 --> 00:34:24,120
If you can hear me,

386
00:34:26,239 --> 00:34:28,080
there's something I want to tell you.

387
00:34:28,679 --> 00:34:31,080
Get up here and make your dream come true.

388
00:34:32,960 --> 00:34:34,199
I'm sorry…

389
00:34:36,239 --> 00:34:40,159
for everything I've done to you.

390
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:48,280
If having me here makes you uncomfortable,

391
00:34:48,360 --> 00:34:50,159
I'll leave.

392
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:53,480
But I want you to know that

393
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:56,560
what we felt for each other…

394
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:01,320
was real.

395
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:09,880
I really love you,

396
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:13,600
and it has nothing to do with any curse.

397
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:17,400
Every moment we spent together…

398
00:35:20,280 --> 00:35:22,360
really made me happy.

399
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:25,800
Please come up and sing.

400
00:35:27,520 --> 00:35:29,000
Come and sing your song.

401
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:33,720
If the music and this band

402
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:35,840
still mean something to you,

403
00:35:40,520 --> 00:35:42,640
please come up and sing.

404
00:35:55,240 --> 00:35:56,480
Well said, man!

405
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:00,760
Khobfa!

406
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:03,160
Can you hear him?

407
00:36:04,040 --> 00:36:05,400
Come on out!

408
00:36:07,440 --> 00:36:09,520
Khobfa!

409
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:12,600
Khobfa!

410
00:36:12,680 --> 00:36:15,440
Khobfa!

411
00:36:15,520 --> 00:36:17,560
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

412
00:36:17,640 --> 00:36:19,360
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

413
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:21,200
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

414
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:24,400
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

415
00:36:24,480 --> 00:36:27,200
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

416
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:30,520
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

417
00:36:30,600 --> 00:36:35,880
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

418
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:39,120
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

419
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:42,560
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

420
00:36:42,640 --> 00:36:46,640
- Khobfa!
- Khobfa!

421
00:36:46,720 --> 00:36:47,680
I still do!

422
00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:16,360
It's not just the music
or the band I have feelings for.

423
00:37:18,600 --> 00:37:20,440
I have feelings for you too, Rin.

424
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:29,480
Then why did you pretend
you didn't remember me?

425
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:32,560
I was afraid
you'd get hurt even more, Rin.

426
00:37:34,800 --> 00:37:36,880
So I had to play along.

427
00:37:36,960 --> 00:37:39,000
I pretended I'd forgotten you.

428
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:45,120
But I never forgot you,
not even for a second.

429
00:37:46,640 --> 00:37:48,760
I kept trying to get close to you,

430
00:37:49,360 --> 00:37:52,720
hoping that one day,
you'd want to tell me the truth,

431
00:37:54,320 --> 00:37:56,000
so we could start over.

432
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:13,680
This next song…

433
00:38:14,800 --> 00:38:19,000
expresses everything I feel about you.

434
00:38:23,520 --> 00:38:27,280
<i>Wake up to the same old things</i>

435
00:38:27,360 --> 00:38:30,840
<i>And the world is never kind</i>

436
00:38:31,400 --> 00:38:34,360
<i>Feels like I did some wrong things</i>

437
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:39,080
<i>Even heaven's not on my side</i>

438
00:38:39,160 --> 00:38:42,680
<i>Everybody says that I</i>

439
00:38:43,240 --> 00:38:46,720
<i>Bring bad luck, whatever I try</i>

440
00:38:47,320 --> 00:38:51,040
<i>No one wants to stick around</i>

441
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:53,960
<i>Or walk by my side</i>

442
00:39:00,640 --> 00:39:04,560
<i>Maybe I'm a man who is so unlucky</i>

443
00:39:04,640 --> 00:39:08,400
<i>Like I've been cursed</i>
<i>And everything gets messy</i>

444
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:11,440
<i>Whatever I do ends in heartache</i>

445
00:39:11,520 --> 00:39:15,000
<i>Disappointment is my only friend</i>

446
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:20,280
<i>But there's still one thing</i>
<i>That somehow turned out right</i>

447
00:39:20,360 --> 00:39:24,440
<i>Whatever comes</i>
<i>I know you'll be there by my side</i>

448
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:27,200
<i>No matter how unlucky life may be</i>

449
00:39:27,280 --> 00:39:30,400
<i>I've got one silver lining on my side</i>

450
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:34,800
<i>I'm lucky enough to have you in my life</i>

451
00:39:36,720 --> 00:39:40,480
<i>From now on, whatever comes</i>

452
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:44,480
<i>But if I have you close to me</i>

453
00:39:44,560 --> 00:39:47,960
<i>No matter how hard the road is</i>

454
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:52,080
<i>I'll keep going if you walk with me</i>

455
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:56,400
<i>Never ever thought that I</i>

456
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:59,920
<i>Bring bad luck, whatever I try</i>

457
00:40:00,480 --> 00:40:04,360
<i>Could have you with me in my life</i>

458
00:40:04,440 --> 00:40:07,440
<i>Never leaving my side</i>

459
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:11,560
<i>But there's still one thing</i>
<i>That somehow turned out right</i>

460
00:40:11,640 --> 00:40:15,280
<i>Whatever comes</i>
<i>I know you'll be there by my side</i>

461
00:40:15,360 --> 00:40:18,360
<i>No matter how unlucky life may be</i>

462
00:40:18,440 --> 00:40:22,000
<i>I've got one silver lining on my side</i>

463
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:28,120
<i>I'm lucky enough to have you in my life</i>

464
00:41:00,320 --> 00:41:04,760
If I had to live with bad luck
without a single lucky break,

465
00:41:05,520 --> 00:41:06,720
I could live with that.

466
00:41:08,600 --> 00:41:10,760
But having bad luck

467
00:41:11,520 --> 00:41:12,800
and not having you?

468
00:41:13,600 --> 00:41:15,000
I couldn't live with that.

469
00:41:20,240 --> 00:41:22,440
I'm blushing for them.

470
00:41:23,760 --> 00:41:28,120
Will you finally take this unlucky guy
as your boyfriend?

471
00:41:28,720 --> 00:41:31,840
There he goes.

472
00:41:47,880 --> 00:41:49,080
Of course!

473
00:41:55,080 --> 00:41:57,760
- They're so sweet together!
- Aw!

474
00:42:02,720 --> 00:42:05,240
Thank you so much, little boy.

475
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:08,080
You're so big, huh?

476
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:18,200
We now have the results
right here in our hands.

477
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:22,360
The two bands with the highest scores are…

478
00:42:22,440 --> 00:42:26,360
- The Winner!
- Sakit!

479
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:28,520
The Winner!

480
00:42:33,600 --> 00:42:35,840
The Winner!

481
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:48,160
And the other band is…

482
00:42:50,040 --> 00:42:52,600
SAKIT, HORIZON, STAND STILL, THE WINNER

483
00:42:52,680 --> 00:42:56,760
- Horizon!
- Horizon!

484
00:42:58,160 --> 00:42:59,840
Horizon!

485
00:43:00,800 --> 00:43:01,760
Shit.

486
00:43:01,840 --> 00:43:03,400
We made it!

487
00:43:08,240 --> 00:43:10,320
That's amazing.

488
00:43:11,080 --> 00:43:16,240
And the champion
of the Campus Stage 2026 is…

489
00:43:16,320 --> 00:43:19,360
SAKIT, HORIZON, STAND STILL, THE WINNER

490
00:43:19,440 --> 00:43:24,320
- The Winner!
- The Winner!

491
00:43:31,960 --> 00:43:36,400
Horizon!

492
00:43:41,800 --> 00:43:45,520
May we invite the judges onstage
to present the award, please?

493
00:43:49,720 --> 00:43:50,720
Congratulations.

494
00:43:54,160 --> 00:43:55,920
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

495
00:44:00,280 --> 00:44:04,120
THE CAMPUS STAGE
100,000 BAHT

496
00:44:07,160 --> 00:44:09,240
THE 5 FINALIST BANDS!

497
00:44:11,800 --> 00:44:13,440
Thank you for coming to see us play,

498
00:44:14,320 --> 00:44:17,760
even though our band lost.

499
00:44:19,840 --> 00:44:21,280
You came second.

500
00:44:22,280 --> 00:44:24,120
You still beat plenty of other bands.

501
00:44:26,000 --> 00:44:26,880
Dad.

502
00:44:27,920 --> 00:44:29,000
You did well.

503
00:44:30,520 --> 00:44:32,240
Send me some clips, okay?

504
00:44:32,840 --> 00:44:34,480
I want to show them to my friends.

505
00:44:35,080 --> 00:44:35,920
Sure.

506
00:44:36,440 --> 00:44:38,360
Your dad cares a lot about you, Krit.

507
00:44:38,440 --> 00:44:40,200
He kept asking about you

508
00:44:40,280 --> 00:44:42,360
and secretly watching
your rehearsal clips.

509
00:44:42,440 --> 00:44:44,600
That's enough. You talk too much.

510
00:44:46,400 --> 00:44:49,000
- Come on. Let's take a picture.
- Come.

511
00:44:50,040 --> 00:44:51,400
I'll take it for you.

512
00:44:51,480 --> 00:44:52,800
No need.

513
00:44:52,880 --> 00:44:56,480
It's a family photo.
Everyone has to be in it.

514
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:05,440
Thank you so much
for not giving up on my son.

515
00:45:08,880 --> 00:45:10,480
Come and join the photo.

516
00:45:12,200 --> 00:45:14,480
One, two, three.

517
00:45:14,560 --> 00:45:17,640
One, two, three. One more.

518
00:45:24,760 --> 00:45:26,440
Where the hell is Rin?

519
00:45:26,520 --> 00:45:28,400
He'll probably be here soon.

520
00:45:28,480 --> 00:45:30,880
Ohm, don't eat everything
before he gets here.

521
00:45:32,440 --> 00:45:33,640
I know, I know.

522
00:45:35,080 --> 00:45:36,040
Hey, Khobfa.

523
00:45:36,120 --> 00:45:38,240
You can't stop smiling, huh?

524
00:45:39,160 --> 00:45:40,200
You keep smiling.

